00:30:31.380 --> 00:30:36.660
So Gladiator meets Mad Max is kind of interesting because Gladiator was like a best picture.

00:30:36.660 --> 00:30:39.940
That's basically just Mad Max Thunderdome though.

00:30:40.220 --> 00:30:42.180
Like you don't need to mix it with anything.

00:30:42.580 --> 00:30:48.800
Right. Peters, who I don't know who that is, but he's the guy who commented on this quote.

00:30:48.980 --> 00:30:55.040
He said that the action oriented film would appeal to a general audience and that the movie

00:30:55.040 --> 00:30:57.280
was going to be a tentpole movie.

00:30:58.360 --> 00:31:00.540
You couldn't say more generic things.

00:31:00.780 --> 00:31:04.500
Like we're going to appeal to a wide audience and this is going to be a blockbuster.

00:31:04.700 --> 00:31:06.400
It's going to start Dennis Quaid.

00:31:07.420 --> 00:31:08.360
I can see that.

00:31:08.640 --> 00:31:13.860
And it was even, it even had a graphic novel in the works too, as part of the media franchise's

00:31:13.860 --> 00:31:15.400
release. So I think that's...

00:31:15.400 --> 00:31:16.780
Oh man, I wonder what happened to Joust.

00:31:16.780 --> 00:31:20.120
Well, you know what's funny there, Sean, is I couldn't help but think about this as

00:31:20.120 --> 00:31:25.600
I was gathering this together, that this is a lot like what we talked about in the Ghostbusters

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:27.740
episode that you mentioned.

00:31:27.900 --> 00:31:31.240
Like, you know, these things are just planned in advance for all these movies.

00:31:31.380 --> 00:31:36.140
Like they get together the book deals, the toys, like they just plan for these movies to

00:31:36.140 --> 00:31:39.420
be giant successes regardless when there's enough money behind them.

00:31:39.760 --> 00:31:45.180
But Joust was never made with the idea that there would be a movie later.

00:31:45.180 --> 00:31:47.060
I mean, that's different.

00:31:47.940 --> 00:31:50.080
I don't know. He was studying a lot about birds.

00:31:50.220 --> 00:31:51.640
Maybe he was studying movies too.

00:31:52.960 --> 00:31:54.860
He was reading how to make a movie.

00:31:56.060 --> 00:31:57.840
That's true. It's just pictures.

00:31:58.120 --> 00:31:59.920
Yep. It's just pictures at the end of the day.

00:32:00.260 --> 00:32:04.780
The only thing we really do on this podcast that's meaningful is the Essential Games list.

00:32:04.780 --> 00:32:06.580
So I think we should do it right now.

00:32:09.300 --> 00:32:12.520
All right. And we're back from that very quick music sting.

00:32:12.520 --> 00:32:15.520
You're probably wondering why I even segue between the two.

00:32:15.720 --> 00:32:19.640
It's it's I should stop using the song altogether and just say let's vote.

00:32:19.920 --> 00:32:22.700
But with that. No, I like I like the rhythm of it.

00:32:22.800 --> 00:32:25.520
OK, that's good. I'm glad that somebody appreciates it.

00:32:26.120 --> 00:32:29.920
So, Sean, since you like it, will you also vote first for us?

00:32:30.040 --> 00:32:32.840
I know that this is not going to be an essential game.

00:32:33.140 --> 00:32:34.620
I enjoyed it enough.

00:32:34.800 --> 00:32:39.320
I'm not even sure if it lives up to my standards for what an essential game should be.

00:32:40.560 --> 00:32:45.360
But I enjoyed this more than Balloon Fight and Balloon Fight's on the essential games list.

00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:51.080
So by that logic, I'm going to vote for it with the understanding that it's going to lose in the end.

00:32:51.260 --> 00:32:53.980
Are you allowed to manipulate the vote like that?

00:32:54.740 --> 00:32:57.540
Are you allowed to like meta vote on the essential?

00:32:57.540 --> 00:32:58.400
No, no, no, no.

00:32:58.400 --> 00:33:00.180
I can vote however I want.

00:33:00.400 --> 00:33:03.460
I'm just saying that I know you guys are not going to vote it on.

00:33:03.460 --> 00:33:09.460
Well, what's funny is there's nothing stopping me and Joe from being like, well, we'll show him and just go and vote it on him.

00:33:09.700 --> 00:33:10.900
But that's his plan.

00:33:10.900 --> 00:33:13.820
If you want to be petty with the essential games list, go right ahead.

00:33:13.940 --> 00:33:15.900
That's his plan. He knows how petty we are.

00:33:16.100 --> 00:33:17.620
He's trying to get it on the essential games list.

00:33:17.700 --> 00:33:22.780
Sean, you don't need to appease the Joust fans out there and put it on the essential games list.

00:33:22.780 --> 00:33:25.200
No, I'm appeasing myself. And that's the only person I need to appease.

00:33:25.420 --> 00:33:27.400
May I take my vote?

00:33:28.360 --> 00:33:33.260
So, Sean, I don't want there to be misunderstanding that I dislike this game.

00:33:33.360 --> 00:33:34.740
I do like this game.

00:33:34.840 --> 00:33:37.060
I did initially have issues with it.

00:33:37.140 --> 00:33:41.240
But the more I got used to it, the more I got the hang of it, I see why it's a fun game.

00:33:41.400 --> 00:33:43.960
And I think if I were to get really good at it, I would...

00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:45.920
You see why it's fun. You don't think it's fun.

00:33:46.160 --> 00:33:47.880
I didn't think it was fun at the beginning.

00:33:48.260 --> 00:33:51.520
But as I played it more, I see why people find it fun.

00:33:51.620 --> 00:33:55.220
And I think if I got better at it, I would find it pretty fun.

00:33:55.220 --> 00:34:02.640
But I think for me, it suffers from a lot of things that arcade games like this suffer from.

00:34:02.740 --> 00:34:05.080
Where it just, to me, just gets repetitive after a while.

00:34:05.520 --> 00:34:10.860
It's, I don't know, it doesn't hold my attention for long enough that I think that it's a must play.

00:34:10.860 --> 00:34:13.240
And I personally liked Balloon Fight more.

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:16.660
And I didn't vote Balloon Fight onto the essential games list.

00:34:16.820 --> 00:34:20.120
So, using the same logic, I will have to not vote it on.

00:34:20.260 --> 00:34:24.780
You know, by all of this logic, it seems like I'm going to have to re-listen to that Balloon Fight episode.

00:34:24.780 --> 00:34:28.060
