I feel like I need to explain myself here.

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:46.940
I have a bullet...

00:34:46.940 --> 00:34:50.160
You don't need to explain. I have a bullet point in my notes here that says,

00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:52.320
Ever feel like you're playing a game the wrong way?

00:34:52.460 --> 00:34:54.580
And I tried to direct that conversation there.

00:34:54.700 --> 00:34:57.200
I don't think Joust is a bad game at all.

00:34:57.300 --> 00:34:59.500
I think I was playing it wrong.

00:34:59.940 --> 00:35:02.100
And I think we solved that here on the show.

00:35:02.220 --> 00:35:06.920
But I don't think I'm going to, like, magically go back to my NES and discover, like,

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:09.760
Oh, yeah, if you play slow, this game is so much more fun.

00:35:09.860 --> 00:35:11.560
Like, I don't think I'm going to uncover that either.

00:35:11.560 --> 00:35:16.840
But my complaints with Joust were mostly on, like, a me level.

00:35:17.260 --> 00:35:22.680
Like, something about this game that took a formula that I clearly liked enough about

00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:24.380
Balloon Fight to put it on the Essential Games list.

00:35:24.400 --> 00:35:27.320
And I actually would... I would still fight for Balloon Fight to this day.

00:35:27.980 --> 00:35:30.760
You know, so I think there's something about Joust that's just...

00:35:30.760 --> 00:35:33.620
It's not quite cutting it for me.

00:35:34.200 --> 00:35:40.300
And I think it has to do with that fast and stiff approach that I was talking about.

00:35:40.300 --> 00:35:46.780
But I will definitely try it again and play it slower and just more methodical, maybe.

00:35:47.060 --> 00:35:50.300
And see if that changes my opinion of it.

00:35:50.360 --> 00:35:52.340
See if I can make it more into Balloon Fight.

00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:57.300
But then that asks the question, should I really be playing Joust if I'm just trying to make it, like, Balloon Fight?

00:35:57.340 --> 00:35:59.240
So it's not an essential game to me.

00:35:59.940 --> 00:36:01.200
I do think it's a good game.

00:36:01.200 --> 00:36:03.780
And I can understand why some would say it's a great game.

00:36:03.920 --> 00:36:07.720
I do think it's weird that we have an arcade game here that so many people talk about.

00:36:08.220 --> 00:36:09.880
And that is really well-liked.

00:36:09.880 --> 00:36:11.720
But has very few sequels.

00:36:11.940 --> 00:36:16.080
And Midway just kind of, like, said, eh, screw it with the rest of Joust's future.

